 "stop": "20 lines",
 "poem": "On the isle of Sarsunya lay\nThe little town, as near alone,\nMaiden-land where all women\nWere given to pluck and ordain;\nAnd when the summer was done before\nAll her days were over again,\nOr with a child's delight started\nFor to leave her country again,\nShe would go; for she had already\nCircumcised her hands, by blessing,\nTo consecrate them to her father\nAs He will bless us again.\nOne day up among the pines standing,\nO'er the waters the river,\nA few steps below him lying,\nHer mother sat in despair,\nLying on his breast alone.\n\"Ah! Mother!\" said the Maidenswoman, crying,\n\"I have no heart left to loving.\nMy mind is like a flower dying,",
